&lt;p&gt;You will work on thought leadership demonstrations and prototypes that push the boundaries of Esri’s geospatial tools and technology, with an emphasis on applying web-based ArcGIS capabilities in new and creative ways. You would be working within a diverse team creating prototypical applications informed by real-world use cases and customer needs to creatively apply Esri’s geospatial technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain prototype applications and proofs of concept using JavaScript, TypeScript, and ArcGIS Maps SDK for JavaScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design and implementation of user experiences for web applications, digital cartographic visualizations, and interactive map-based workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in prototyping and experimenting with novel web-based maps, scenes, and spatial data visualizations, helping explore how geospatial information can be effectively represented in browser-based contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with modern web application frameworks such as React, Angular, Svelte, or Vue to build targeted, stand-alone web applications and reusable UI components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with core development and SDK teams during release development sprints, providing feedback on APIs, beta capabilities, tools, workflows, documentation, and developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore and apply emerging web visualization capabilities, including WebGL and browser-based real-time visualization, to support advanced 2D, 3D, and multidimensional spatial experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve coding and development skills by staying current with JavaScript, TypeScript, complementary programming languages, development practices, coding tools, and user interface design techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience developing web applications using JavaScript; TypeScript experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern web application frameworks such as React, Angular, Vue, Svelte, or similar technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with code management systems and CI/CD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of digital cartography, data visualization, or geospatial application development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, engineering, mathematics, GIS, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel domestically or internationally up to 25–50%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visa sponsorship is not available for this posting. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ArcGIS Maps SDK for JavaScript, ArcGIS Experience Builder, or other Esri web technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in geospatial technology and applying innovative approaches to solve complex visualization and application development challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with WebGL, 3D visualization, or browser-based real-time rendering technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in computer science, engineering, mathematics, GIS, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
