&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of work experience with master purchasing agreements, enterprise programs, proposals, quotes, and/or contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience with commercial software pricing models, strategy, pricing analysis and/or pricing catalogs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Esri product models, licensing, and maintenance programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the software sales process, software licensing, software, intellectual property, and basic contract structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clarify complex business relationships through research and consultation with multiple stakeholders in addition to maintaining confidentiality of pricing, reporting, and terms of contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, interpersonal, and listening skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail oriented with the ability to work with a high level of accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with Microsoft Office applications, particularly reporting functionality and spreadsheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional travel may be required (up to ~10%); travel needs may vary based on business requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in business, management, economics, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
