&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help Protect the People, Programs, and Environments Supporting Critical National Security Missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join Esri`s Industrial Security team as a Facility Security Officer (FSO), supporting classified programs and secure operations across our federal business. You`ll help administer industrial security requirements, maintain compliant secure environments, and partner with government customers, program teams, and employees to enable mission execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We`re looking for an experienced industrial security professional who understands the cleared contractor environment and can independently manage complex security responsibilities while serving as a trusted resource to employees, leadership, and government partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Esri`s Industrial Security Programs in accordance with applicable NISPOM and government requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support facility and personnel security requirements for classified programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage clearance, access, visit, briefing, and debriefing process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support DD254 and contract security requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for and support security assessments and inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain security documentation, procedures, records, and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with government security representatives and internal program teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain compliant classified facilities and secure work environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional experience in a similar position, supporting similar responsibilities exemplify&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience conducting special access and industrial security operations for the US DoD or US Intelligence Community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a certified FSO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience as a CSSO (or CPSO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough working knowledge of the NISPOM, ICDs, associated Executive Orders, and Security Executive Agent Directives (SEADs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience with the DISS/NBIS, NISS, SWFT, eQIP/eAPP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of OPSEC procedures and application of OPSEC to Sensitive Government information (FOUO, CUI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess and maintain an active Top Secret security clearance with SCI eligibility and current polygraph&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree in Criminal Justice, Business Administration, Information Systems, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Professional Memberships (NCMS, ISWG, and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ICD 503 Risk Management Framework process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master`s Degree in Criminal Justice, Business Administration, Information Systems, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
