&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and oversee the execution of global go-to-market strategies to drive growth in new and existing markets in the Electric Industry. Your objective is to be the Industry thought leader, drive awareness and demand in target markets, and inspire the community by positioning Esri GIS technology to address existing and emerging industry challenges and opportunities. You will collaborate closely with teams in Business Development, Marketing, Professional Services, Solutions, and Software Development to align industry trends with Esri technology for current and future demand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Esri as the subject matter expert in the Electric Industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position Esri as a thought leader in the Electric Industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast and evaluate industry trends using a variety of data; proactively develop solutions and messages to address key business issues, drivers, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, manage, and execute a comprehensive global marketing strategy for the Electric, Generation, Transmission and Distribution domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create thought leadership content in technical papers, webinars, blogs and customer success stories to demonstrate business value of GIS in the Electric Industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive industry marketing plans, programs, both short and long range, to support the GIS user community and grow the use of GIS in the Electric Industry community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge about competition and customer requirements to enable Business Development teams to be more effective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research, analyze, and monitor technological, and market factors in the Electric Industry to capitalize on service and market opportunities in the domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate, understand, and develop new business in areas underserved or not currently served with GIS applications across an Electric Utility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and recommend product/industry positioning, collateral generation, and support sales and revenue objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product Development as a customer advocate for needs of the Electric Industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with sales staff, international division regional managers, and Esri distributors to provide domain expertise, contacts, support, and guidance for working with the Electric community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the business partner group to recruit, develop, and maintain partners and partner channels to ensure the delivery of solutions to the Electric Industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent and manage Esri’s presence at industry-related conferences, trade shows, seminars, and other events domestically and internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a strong GIS user community within the Electric or Power Industries through printed collateral, e-newsletters, online forums, user groups, and other networking opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate the use of GIS technology to the various the Electric Industry related trade associations, standards organizations, and media&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
