&lt;li&gt;5+ years of proven leadership experience with the ability to motivate, inspire, and achieve goals through a matrix team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GIS technology as uniquely suited to address existing and emerging industry challenges and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of Electric Utility issues, challenges, workflows, and opportunities for improvement using GIS and its practical applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Membership and leadership in industry associations and societies for 5+ years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting Electric initiatives to executives, managers, and influencers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience publishing industry articles, blogs, books, or other thought leadership authorship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in public speaking to organizations representing the industries in the Electric Industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel both domestically and internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, GIS, geography, computer science, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
