&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leverage your payroll expertise to oversee daily payroll operations, drive process and system improvements, and lead the development of a high-performing team of payroll professionals. In this role, you will ensure accurate and compliant payroll processing, enhance operational efficiencies, and support departmental goals through effective leadership, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our busy collaborative team onsite at our stunning campus in Redlands, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise day-to-day processing of multi-state US payroll, including compliance with federal/state laws and regulations and company policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with payroll vendor to ensure timeliness and accuracy of all tax filings and amendments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise payroll representatives, including reviewing and assigning workload, assuring quality control for processes, conducting performance reviews for direct reports, and resolving any issues that may arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support payroll system upgrade testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integration with HR and timekeeping systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend process changes to improve efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Function as back up to direct report staff and/or Payroll Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of payroll experience including federal, state, and local employment tax, reciprocity, quarterly and year-end tax return, and information filing, including 2+ years of supervision or lead experience including assignment and review of work and conducting performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a major HCM application, including HR, timekeeping, payroll, and reporting modules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of payroll administration processes, procedures, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal skills, including diplomacy, negotiating, reasoning, and problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated strong analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how payroll processes impact accounting transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visa sponsorship is not available for this posting. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in business, accounting, finance, human resources, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
