&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launch your career in process improvement by supporting the identification, documentation, and optimization of business processes. As a Process Analyst, you will work closely with experienced team members to map processes, analyze data, and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives. This entry-level role is designed to build foundational skills in process analysis, stakeholder engagement, and professional communication, providing a pathway for growth within the Process Improvement team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and interpret process maps (such as SIPOC, swimlane diagrams) using organizational standards and tools; accurately capture process steps, roles, handoffs, and decision points&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in pain point analysis sessions, capturing and categorizing process inefficiencies and frustrations; apply Lean principles to identify improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the application of basic root cause analysis techniques (such as 5 Whys) to understand underlying drivers of process issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to brainstorming sessions for potential solutions, focusing on identifying and articulating clear actions and anticipated benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the collection and analysis of relevant process data (cycle times, volumes, error rates) to support problem definition and solution validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and organize key process improvement artifacts, such as problem statements, current state analyses, solution outlines, and implementation plans, adhering to organizational templates and quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively listen to stakeholders, ask clarifying and probing questions, and synthesize diverse perspectives to support effective communication and stakeholder engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin developing facilitation skills for small group discussions or presenting findings on process segments or quick win proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate proactively with process owners, subject matter experts, and the Process Excellence team to support cross-functional initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate adaptability, openness to feedback, and a willingness to learn new tools and concepts rapidly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit professionalism in all interactions, proactively seek opportunities to contribute, manage time effectively, and take ownership of assigned tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of full-time work experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training or exposure to Business Process Management (BPM) tools and methodologies; adherence to established standards and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or training in process mapping, modeling, and reengineering, including mapping current and ideal processes and identifying improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to process improvement, consulting basics, and participation in team-based problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic facilitation skills and ability to overcome simple obstacles in meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work well with others, share ideas, and show initiative in team settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with process flow diagrams and basic process design concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong documentation skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical and problem-solving mindset, with a willingness to learn and adapt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate appropriate security and data privacy safeguards into work activities, communications and deliverables to protect sensitive, confidential and regulated information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s in Business, Information Systems, Industrial Engineering, Operations Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training or coursework in Lean, Six Sigma, or Business Process Management (BPM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with process mapping tools (such as Microsoft Visio, LucidChart)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to data collection and analysis for process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
