&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Product Engineer passionate about software development, APIs, and web technologies. In this role, you’ll design, test, and document REST API features in collaboration with cross-functional engineering and product teams. You’ll help ensure ArcGIS Enterprise REST APIs are reliable, secure, scalable, and designed to solve real customer problems. This role blends strong technical skills with user advocacy, clear documentation, and cross-team communication to deliver REST API features that power critical GIS workflows for organizations worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, design, test, certify, release, and support ArcGIS Online&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with various development teams to build new capabilities and improve existing workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform functional and workflow driven testing (manual and automated) to assess product quality and readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and understand issues with security, internationalization, and accessibility in new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather requirements from users and teams within Esri and distill them into meaningful product features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write conceptual documentation, guided tutorials, and blogs for the features we build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an advocate for the user and represent the user in product design and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One (1) year of experience in the job offered, or one (1) year of experience in a related occupation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must demonstrate Java, ArcGIS Online, Python, C#, ArcGIS Pro, and REST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree, or foreign equivalent degree, in GIS, Computer Science or a related field &lt;/li&gt;
