&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join Esri&#39;s Information Systems and Technology (IST) division and help shape the future of product operations and release readiness across the organization. As a Product Engineer II supporting business applications, you will serve as a product and platform steward for Esri&#39;s enterprise product operations platform, guiding its roadmap, governance, adoption, and continued evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary focus will be an Airtable-based platform that centralizes product business rules, release planning, operational change requirements, workflow management, task tracking, and readiness activities across multiple business units. You will combine platform expertise, product thinking, and cross-functional collaboration to improve operational outcomes, strengthen data and process consistency, and help teams successfully adopt new capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a product and platform steward for the business application supporting product operations and organizational release readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Owners and operational stakeholders to identify process needs, define desired outcomes, and prioritize platform improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the intake and evaluation of enhancement requests, balancing stakeholder impact, dependencies, governance requirements, and long-term platform health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and optimize platform workflows, automations, interfaces, and business rules that improve the consistency and efficiency of product operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate operational readiness activities for platform changes, including acceptance criteria, user validation, documentation, communication, launch support, and post-release review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and prioritize the platform backlog and contribute to roadmap planning based on operational impact, stakeholder needs, risk, and organizational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain governance standards for platform configuration, product business rules, data quality, access, documentation, and change control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee product information workflows across Airtable, ServiceNow, and related enterprise platforms, helping ensure reliable data exchange, clear ownership, and alignment with established business rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor platform health, adoption, data quality, and workflow effectiveness to identify risks, recurring issues, and opportunities for continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop enablement resources and provide guidance that helps stakeholders effectively use platform capabilities and follow established operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new platform, automation, and AI capabilities and recommend applications that improve product operations and release readiness outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate post-launch reviews, gather stakeholder feedback, and translate findings into prioritized platform and process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain product documentation, knowledge articles, governance guidance, support resources, and operational procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
