&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us for a fast-paced and challenging career where you can combine your passion for software development, APIs, and the web. The ArcGIS Online team is a key part of the ArcGIS platform that&#39;s transforming how geographic data is used and empowering users to leverage GIS like never before. As a Product Engineer, you&#39;ll design and test new features, communicate best practices for using the REST API for content management, and enhance product usability. This role offers the opportunity to innovate and make a real impact on a platform that shapes the future of GIS technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with the front-end development team:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Work with front-end developers to design, define, and optimize APIs that support key features in ArcGIS Online content items, groups, and users, ensuring performance and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Author and maintain REST API documentation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Write and update clear, detailed API documentation, including sample code and guidelines for efficient use and integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and implement automation testing:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Create automated test scripts to validate API performance and reliability, integrating them into CI pipelines for continuous quality checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage software quality issues from users and internal teams&lt;/strong&gt;: Address and resolve reported bugs, coordinating with support teams to ensure quick and accurate fixes while improving overall product stability&lt;/li&gt;
