&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ArcGIS Earth&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;a product used by hundreds of thousands of users across desktop and mobile devices that gives access to 3D maps anywhere.&amp;nbsp;In this role, you&amp;nbsp;will&amp;nbsp;identify&amp;nbsp;and prioritize industry requirements for a product effort charged with defining, building, and releasing ArcGIS Earth, a lightweight, easy-to-use client application for users to browse maps, explore 3D content,&amp;nbsp;and share information.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will focus on the use of ArcGIS Earth within large enterprise user communities in federal and state government. You will be expected to find and realize&amp;nbsp;additional&amp;nbsp;opportunities for ArcGIS Earth to bring the value of ArcGIS into everyday user workflows including related technologies such as imagery, IoT, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize user needs and market opportunities through interviews, research and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the product plan and roadmap based on customer feedback and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Engineers to develop product specifications and user stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other product managers to align the vision for reality mapping with market and organizational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure teams are prepared for product releases, including sales and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Global Business Development and partners are equipped to engage with potential customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the go-to expert on reality mapping capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and implementation of pricing and licensing strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster collaboration across teams to ensure a cohesive product story and success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Marketing to plan and deliver effective go-to-market strategies, product messaging and release communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote GIS and 3D through presentations and publications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep knowledge of open specifications and standards, including KML/KMZ, i3S, 3DTiles and other OGC standards to support key markets and to recommend changes and additions to help standard adoption internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of practical experience in the geospatial field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a Product Manager or similar role, preferably in the geospatial technology or mapping industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, storytelling, and persuasion skills across all levels of an organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of GIS, 3D, and engineering technology for visualization, collaboration, situational awareness, or planning&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in federal government GIS operations with a focus on defense and law enforcement workflows&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to present to customers and to cultivate strategic relationships with customers and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;U.S. citizenship with the ability and willingness to obtain a security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requirement for travel 10-20% for strategic meetings, events, and/or tradeshows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in GIS, Geospatial Technology, Geography, Computer Science or STEM related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical experience using business analytic software, data transformations, and new technologies in the area of data analytics and visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with geospatial technology, mapping, and location-based content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Pragmatic Marketing Framework&lt;/li&gt;
