&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer, you will work with our cross-functional global team of software engineers, product engineers, designers, product managers, and release engineers. You will be actively involved in enhancing the capability of the ArcGIS Enterprise platform from feature inception to delivery, using bleeding edge technology. If you are building great distributed systems, micro-services architecture, and spatial data analytics, join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the next generation of ArcGIS Business Analyst Enterprise, a product delivering state-of-the-art mapping and analytics capabilities to thousands of customers and users worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build highly-scalable and reliable distributed software for on-premises and the cloud to make maps, geographic information, and analyses available on any device, anywhere, at any time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide a strong technical voice in the product development process and use the best tools available to design, develop, and deliver a high-quality distributed systems platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a cross-functional global team of software engineers, product engineers, designers, product managers, and release engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance the capability of the ArcGIS Enterprise platform from feature inception to delivery, using bleeding edge technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support web services components that follow industry-standard design patterns, development methodologies, and deployment models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build server-side Java components and web services to power user experience and geospatial workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype, design, develop, and deliver complete software features and products that can scale, are fault tolerant, and handle concurrent workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, architect, and build complete software features/products and underlying geospatial databases to meet customer requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find, analyze, and fix bugs/performance problems whenever and wherever they occur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with other teams to understand requirements and incorporate them into the software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Five (5) years of progressive, post-baccalaureate experience in the job offered, or five (5) years of progressive, post-baccalaureate experience in a related occupation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must demonstrate experience in C++, Python, Agile Software Development, Esri ArcObjects, ArcGIS Enterprise, RDBMS, Data Localization, and ArcGIS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree, or foreign equivalent degree, in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, GIS, or a related field &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
