&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esri is the world leader in geographic information systems (GIS) and the developer of ArcGIS, the leading mapping and analytics platform used by organizations worldwide. Our teams build highly scalable, secure, and reliable ArcGIS Enterprise capabilities for on-premises and cloud environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Build and DevOps Engineer, you will help design, automate, and maintain the systems that build, test, package, deploy, and operate ArcGIS Enterprise software. You will work closely with software developers, product engineers, release engineers to improve build reliability, release velocity, system stability, and operational excellence across global development environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and maintain reliable build, packaging, and release automation for ArcGIS Enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate software delivery, infrastructure provisioning, configuration management, and environment lifecycle operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automation using Python, PowerShell, Shell, or other scripting languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage build artifacts, dependencies, versioning, configuration, and release metadata across development and delivery pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with development and QA teams to improve application testability, build performance, and release readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor pipeline health, infrastructure stability, system performance, and deployment outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve build, deployment, infrastructure, and environment-related issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate effectively with distributed teams and help drive alignment across engineering, release, and IT organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in build engineering, DevOps, release engineering, system administration, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and maintaining CI/CD pipelines and software delivery automation using Jenkins and/or GitHub Actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python, PowerShell, Shell or another scripting language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Docker and Kubernetes or similar container orchestration technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of software build, packaging, deployment, and release processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting complex software, infrastructure, and automation issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fundamental understanding of REST APIs, networking, and distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with cross-functional and geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, information technology, engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing infrastructure-as-code solutions using Terraform, CloudFormation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with configuration-management tools such as Ansible&lt;/li&gt;
