&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you an experienced contracts professional looking to take the next step in your career? Join Esri&#39;s Professional Services division as a Sr. Contract Specialist and play a key role in shaping agreements that support our mission to deliver transformative geospatial solutions. In this role, you&#39;ll manage a variety of complex contracts, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and provide guidance on contract structuring and compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be joining a team of experienced professionals who enjoy working together to support Esri&#39;s large customer base and internal customer requests. We love what we do, and we love Esri&#39;s philosophy. You will have a management team and colleagues who are here to support you. Technology is always changing, and our customers are finding new ways to utilize geospatial software to improve the world, so your assignments are varied, challenging and fascinating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Esri has a Relocation Assistance Program and can provide support with relocating to the Redlands, CA area for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full lifecycle of services contracts, including RFP analysis, proposal development, negotiation, execution, and closeout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance to internal stakeholders on contract terms, risk mitigation, and compliance with applicable regulations and policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with legal, finance, and project teams to resolve contractual issues and support program success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support a variety of contract types, including commercial, public sector, international, and federal agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development and improvement of contract management practices and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply knowledge of FAR/DFAR and federal procurement processes where applicable; federal experience is highly valued but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in contract administration, with increasing responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in negotiating and managing a variety of contract types and structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of contract law, risk management, and procurement best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in business administration, legal studies, political science, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be authorized to work in the US; visa sponsorship is not available for this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
