&lt;li&gt;Become an ArcGIS Enterprise Business Analyst extension technical expert and collaborate with software developers, product engineers, product managers, and other stakeholders to determine product quality and release readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the software product life cycle by contributing to software requirements definition, continuous improvement processes, UX design, testing, documentation, release, and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and track software issues, build reproducible QA scenarios and communicate test results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft product demonstrations, give presentations, create videos, blogs, and supporting materials that guide best practices for users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and prioritize issues from customers, gather requirements from customers and evaluate new features for future releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support software migration and development across enterprise and highly scalable operating environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of multi-national, on-premise data packages and software components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with Esri software including ArcGIS Enterprise, ArcGIS Pro and ArcGIS Online&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal and presentation skills with the ability to communicate complex concepts to a variety of audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of Windows and Linux. Working knowledge of Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the ArcGIS APIs and location services such as GeoEnrichment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging web services and client applications with browser developer tools and tools such as Fiddler&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work fast-paced team environment, but also self-driven to make a difference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in geography, GIS, computer science, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
