&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the Network Diagram team and help shape advanced network visualization and analysis capabilities across ArcGIS. We’re looking for a Senior Product Engineer who combines strong analytical skills, domain curiosity, and a passion for building high-quality, user-centered software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will play a key part in defining, validating, and communicating Network Diagram capabilities, with a strong focus on integration with Utility Network workflows. You will collaborate closely with development teams to refine requirements, influence product design, and ensure a seamless and effective user experience. You will also contribute to the quality of the product through thoughtful validation, exploratory testing, and real-world scenario analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly collaborative role that blends product thinking, domain expertise, and hands-on investigation to deliver meaningful value to our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep expertise in Network Diagrams and Utility Network workflows, contributing to product direction and design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering teams to refine requirements, scenarios, and expected system behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use domain knowledge and AI-assisted analysis to explore workflows, identify gaps, and improve user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate capabilities through exploratory, scenario-based, and data-driven approaches grounded in real-world use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply sound testing practices and use scripting and AI-assisted techniques to improve coverage and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, reproduce, and help resolve issues in collaboration with development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate customer-reported issues using real workflows and AI-assisted analysis to accelerate understanding and resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate product behavior using utility and network scenarios to drive meaningful improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to best practices that support successful customer adoption of Network Diagram capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear, high-quality documentation, guidance, and examples that support user success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate complex technical concepts effectively across teams and to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI-assisted tools to improve clarity, consistency, and efficiency in content and communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a GIS, software development, or related technical environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with network visualization, diagrams, or schematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with utility or telecommunications networks and their data models and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python for scripting and automation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to understand complex systems and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of software quality practices and validation approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of the software development lifecycle and agile methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to explain complex technical concepts clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and ability to drive work independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively use modern tools, including AI-assisted workflows, to enhance productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in GIS, engineering, computer science, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing work authorization for France&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ArcGIS, especially ArcGIS Pro and Utility Network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with relational or geospatial databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in C#&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to technical documentation or user guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with version control systems such as Git&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree (Master’s or PhD) in a relevant field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
