&lt;li&gt;Experience administering ArcGIS Enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with troubleshooting technical issues in server‑based systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to consistently apply a systematic, best‑practice‑driven approach to system engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly communicate technical concepts to customers, executives, and technical and non‑technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Geographic Information Systems (GIS), or a related STEM field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of or interest in additional ArcGIS technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with one or more major cloud providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting and/or programming languages such as shell scripting, Python, PowerShell, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System administration experience with Windows, Linux, and/or Kubernetes platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of or interest in networking concepts including HTTP, TCP, TLS, DNS, firewalls, and proxy technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
